From 8d5fad10b5aa4f46490cc14dadf752eed7cb38ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maximiliano <m.lopz.montn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:28:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: restyle the account screen with the app's design
 system
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AccountScreen was plain unstyled markup (no classes at all beyond a
bare .container), the odd one out next to every other screen in the
app. Rebuild it using the existing tokens/components instead:

- .container-narrow + .surface card, matching PaletteManageScreen
- a real segmented control for Sign in / Create account instead of
  two loose buttons
- .btn-primary / .btn-secondary / .btn-ghost throughout, labels
  properly associated to inputs via htmlFor/id
- a consistent "← Back" btn-ghost in the corner, same as the other
  sub-screens

Also add a small sync-status badge (live/connecting/error) once
signed in, driven by useAccount's new syncStatus, so a broken
real-time connection is visible instead of silent. New CSS lives
under a dedicated 'Account screen' section at the end of index.css.

Fix the 'Account' button in HomeScreen's header, which had no btn
class and looked out of place next to 'Manage Palettes' / '+ New
Pattern'.

All existing AccountScreen tests still pass unmodified assertions
(same copy, same aria-labels, same roles); added cases for the new
sync badge states.
